                "url": "https://github.com/edemaine"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/779047?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds data for the <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/mediaqueries-5/#preferences-attribute\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">navigator.preferences</code></a> property and related.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">N/A</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Refs <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4000297077\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43276\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43276/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43276\">mdn/content#43276</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29142",
            "title": "Add data related to navigator.preferences",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-27T16:01:11.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-27T10:23:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "remcohaszing",
                "url": "https://github.com/remcohaszing"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=2f3b9dd03c6c4a961d44a632fe1976c73fa19e1f&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates the Safari support statements for the <code class=\"notranslate\">loading</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">loadingdone</code>/<code class=\"notranslate\">loadingend</code> events for <code class=\"notranslate\">FontFaceSet</code>: The event handlers are supported, but the events never fire.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304091\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=304091</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/19e24b1ecd033405f93bc3eaf027ecc192f6f459/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/commit/19e24b1ecd033405f93bc3eaf027ecc192f6f459\">WebKit/WebKit@<tt>19e24b1</tt></a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29035.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3932538085\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29035\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29035/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29035\">#29035</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29066",
            "title": "Safari only partially supports `FontFaceSet` loading events",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-23T12:09:25.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-17T20:26:00.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for scroll-triggered animations; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5181996801982464\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5181996801982464</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29033\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29033/hovercard\">latest Chrome collector PR</a> has added BCD for several of the related features; my PR adds a few more, namely the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;animation-action&gt;</code> data type, and the related range properties, which <em>are</em> supported but currently under an old name.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29034",
            "title": "Chrome 146 scroll-triggered animations",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-18T16:46:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-12T15:28:11.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Address is the dev-doc-needed requirements of</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2012727\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2012727</a> \"action.isEnabled() throws instead of returning the global enabled state\", and</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2013477\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 2013477</a> Support action.isEnabled(tabId) next to action.isEnabled(details)<br>\nby, under <code class=\"notranslate\">isEnabled</code>:</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">adding <code class=\"notranslate\">details</code> and moving the information for <code class=\"notranslate\">windowID</code> under it.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p dir=\"auto\">adding note to <code class=\"notranslate\">details</code>regarding support for either an integer (tab ID) or object.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related content changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3887257311\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42997\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42997/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42997\">mdn/content#42997</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28964",
            "title": "Bug-2012727 action.isEnabled updated properties info",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-26T10:35:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-02-03T17:37:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 144 supports the <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> pseudo-element, which allows custom styling to be applied to browser search results; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5195073796177920</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">We already have BCD for <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code>, however, you can combine <code class=\"notranslate\">::search-text</code> with the <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> pseudo-class to style the currently-highlighted search term on the page. This currently doesn't have any BCD, so I am using this PR to add <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> BCD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I'm assuming it makes sense to put Chrome 144 down for this as well, as previously, there was no context in which <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> was supported. However, you might have other opinions on this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also thought about putting <code class=\"notranslate\">\"partial_implementation\": \"true\"</code> for this, but then again, <code class=\"notranslate\">:current</code> is fully supported in the context it is supported in. It just isn't supported in other contexts.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28882",
            "title": "Chrome 144 :current support",
            "date_modified": "2026-02-03T12:43:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-01-21T18:28:23.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">There is updates to add details to cover Safari support for documentId and parentDocumentId. More information on changes see the related content PR. (TBC)</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28341.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3575616610\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28341\">#28341</a><br>\nRelated content changes in (TBC)</p>",
